    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1306">

                <pb facs="1568" n="1370" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/AE Files</note>
                <head>No. 1306<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to the Secretary of
                        War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">and personal</hi></seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary Stimson</hi>[:] I enclose a photostat record of the Hyde
                    Park Agreement on T. A., for which you asked the Chancellor of the
                        Exchequer.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1306-f1"/></p>
                <pb facs="1569" n="1371" xml:id="pg1371"/>
                <p>This photograph was taken by a special photographic section of the Air Ministry,
                    and flown out here in the charge of a trusted officer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">inston</hi>] S
                                C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">hurchill</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-18">18.7.45</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1306-a1.xml" xpointer="d1306-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1306-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1306-f1-content">
                <p>Sir John Anderson. Following the death of
                    President Roosevelt, an authenticated
                    text of the enclosed <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> was not available
                    to responsible American officials. Before the Berlin Conference, Stimson had asked the British Government to
                    supply a photocopy of the <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
